# b2-fit.tr (bonus): the heap has 400 big holes and then 400 small ones.
# 400 small requests arrive, then 400 big ones. A small request is just
# over half a big hole, so first fit (and a LIFO free list, since the big
# holes were freed last) spoils one big hole with each small request,
# and then the big requests fit nowhere. Best fit, or segregated free
# lists, put the small requests in the small holes and the heap does
# not grow.

